"""mrg5-bt-central [hciN]: make the adapter take the central role on incoming connections
(checks/34, "Bluetooth audio"). Run by udev when the adapter appears
(/etc/udev/rules.d/90-mrg5-bt-central.rules).

A DualShock 4 connects to the box by itself after power-on, so the box ended up as the pad's
peripheral while it was central for headphones: two piconets with different masters (a
scatternet), and the controller had to share its time between them. With the pad sending
~100 reports/s, A2DP got 225 kbit/s of the 552 the codec needed and the audio skipped.
With the box central on every link it got 399 (2026-10-03).

This is `hciconfig hci0 lm accept,master`: the HCISETLINKMODE ioctl. The kernel then asks
for the central role when it accepts a connection (net/bluetooth/hci_event.c,
hci_conn_request_evt: mask = hdev->link_mode, cp.role = 0x00 "Become central").
"""
import fcntl
import socket
import struct
import sys

HCISETLINKMODE = 0x400448e2                   # _IOW('H', 226, int)
HCI_LM_ACCEPT, HCI_LM_MASTER = 0x8000, 0x0001

dev = int(sys.argv[1].removeprefix("hci")) if len(sys.argv) > 1 else 0
s = socket.socket(socket.AF_BLUETOOTH, socket.SOCK_RAW, socket.BTPROTO_HCI)
# struct hci_dev_req { __u16 dev_id; __u32 dev_opt; }
fcntl.ioctl(s, HCISETLINKMODE, struct.pack("@HI", dev, HCI_LM_ACCEPT | HCI_LM_MASTER))
print("hci%d: link mode accept,central" % dev)
